IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g1-interpretation`
IMPORT `g1-art1-defined-terms`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-vintages`
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`

-- ind-a-tests-art1.l4: independent tests of Article 1 (interpretation), with the vintages of "Minister" and "Comptroller".
-- Every expected value comes from WORK/ind-a/expectations.md (scenario ids S1-nn), decided from the Law and the amending instruments before the encoding was opened.
-- A day is turned into a text of the Law by G7's resolver (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on`), an instant by `Endnotes: the vintage of the text at`; G1 answers for the text.

§ `ind-a tests: Article 1`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`ind-a Minister on` d MEANS
    `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` d `the favoured interpretation`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      h IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Office of the Minister`
`ind-a Minister at` d h m MEANS
    `Art 1 the Minister under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text at` (DATETIME_FROM_DTZ d (TIME_FROM_HMS h m 0) "Europe/Jersey") `the favoured interpretation`)

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Law defining the Comptroller`
`ind-a Comptroller Law on` d MEANS
    `Art 1 the Law that defines the Comptroller under the text of` (`Endnotes: the vintage of the text on` d `the favoured interpretation`)

GIVEN st IS A `Standing on the register`
GIVETH AN Entity
`ind-a company standing` st MEANS
    `ind-a entity` "Hope Jersey Limited" st (LIST `a company`) TRUE EMPTY EMPTY

§§ `"registered charity" (S1-01 to S1-04)`

-- S1-01 general section -> TRUE (src:34)
#ASSERT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`ind-a company standing` `entered in the general section`)
-- S1-02 restricted section -> TRUE (src:34)
#ASSERT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`ind-a company standing` `entered in the restricted section`)
-- S1-03 historic section only -> FALSE (src:34)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`ind-a company standing` `formerly registered and entered in the historic section`)
-- S1-04 never entered (and an applicant) -> FALSE (src:34)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`ind-a company standing` `not on the register`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the entity is a registered charity` (`ind-a company standing` `an applicant for registration`)

§§ `"publish" (S1-14): the opinion of the person publishing is an input`

`ind-a publication believed adequate but not in fact likely` MEANS
    `Facts about a publication` WITH
        `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
        `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE
        `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE

`ind-a publication not believed adequate` MEANS
    `Facts about a publication` WITH
        `made available by the person in some manner` IS TRUE
        `the person publishing is of the opinion that the manner is likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS FALSE
        `the manner is in fact likely to bring it to the attention of the public or of those affected` IS TRUE

-- src:30: "in the opinion of the person publishing" -> the opinion decides
#ASSERT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `ind-a publication believed adequate but not in fact likely`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 1 the information has been published` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 1 and 2` `ind-a publication not believed adequate`

§§ `"Minister" (S1-15 to S1-32)`

-- S1-15 2014-11-20: the Law is not in force; no answer
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2014 11 20)
-- S1-18 2019-01-01 -> Chief Minister
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2019 1 1) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
-- S1-19 2019-05-30 -> Chief Minister
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2019 5 30) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
-- S1-20 2019-05-31 -> Minister for External Relations (R&O.40/2019)
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2019 5 31) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S1-21 2019-12-16 and 2020-01-01 -> MER
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2019 12 16) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S1-22 2021-03-01 -> MER
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2021 3 1) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S1-23 2021-03-02 -> MERFS (R&O.29/2021)
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2021 3 2) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services`
-- S1-24 2023-04-11 -> MERFS
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2023 4 11) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations and Financial Services`
-- S1-25 2023-04-12 -> Chief Minister (R&O.28/2023)
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2023 4 12) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
-- S1-26 2024-02-26 -> Chief Minister
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2024 2 26) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
-- S1-27 2024-02-27 as a date only -> cannot decide
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2024 2 27)
-- S1-28 instants on 2024-02-27 (Jersey time = GMT in February)
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister at` (YMD 2024 2 27) 9 29 EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister at` (YMD 2024 2 27) 9 30 EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister at` (YMD 2024 2 27) 9 31 EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S1-29 2024-02-28 -> MER
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2024 2 28) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S1-30 2025-10-09 (R&O.56/2025 made) and 2025-10-16 -> MER
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2025 10 9) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2025 10 16) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S1-31 2026-10-01 -> MER
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2026 10 1) EQUALS `the Minister for External Relations`
-- S1-32 2026-10-02 and 2026-10-27 -> Chief Minister (R&O.102/2026)
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2026 10 2) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`
#ASSERT `ind-a Minister on` (YMD 2026 10 27) EQUALS `the Chief Minister`

§§ `"Comptroller" (S1-33)`

-- S1-33 2019-12-31 -> Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961; 2020-01-01 and 2026-10-27 -> Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019 (L.13/2019 Sch 3 para 1; R&O.136/2019)
#ASSERT `ind-a Comptroller Law on` (YMD 2019 12 31) EQUALS `the Income Tax (Jersey) Law 1961`
#ASSERT `ind-a Comptroller Law on` (YMD 2020 1 1) EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT `ind-a Comptroller Law on` (YMD 2026 10 27) EQUALS `the Revenue Administration (Jersey) Law 2019`
#ASSERT REFUSED `ind-a Comptroller Law on` (YMD 2014 11 20)
